        "original_id": "712aeff3-03c3-5541-81d0-b566a02e13f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tedrow, Ohio; Emery, Ohio; Dover Township; Fulton County; Ohio; Chicago; Pittsburgh\n- Transportation infrastructure: Ohio Turnpike; James W. Shocknessy Ohio Turnpike\n- Topics: community location; ghost towns\n\nFacts:\n- The Ohio Turnpike, officially named the James W. Shocknessy Ohio Turnpike, is a 241.26-mile limited-access toll highway in Ohio.\n- The Ohio Turnpike serves as a primary travel corridor to Chicago and Pittsburgh.\n- Tedrow, Ohio, lies less than one mile north of the Ohio Turnpike.\n- The nearest Ohio Turnpike exit to Tedrow is several miles away.\n- Emery, Ohio, is a ghost town in Dover Township, Fulton County, Ohio.\n- Emery, Ohio, is near present-day Tedrow, Ohio.",
